        each.  Drawn iff pn_node_is_processing_visible (honest by
        construction).  Precedence: disabled still wins (an inert node neither
        glows nor errors); a node can plausibly be both busy and have-error --
        decide whether the halo coexists with the red body (likely yes: red
        card + neon halo reads fine) or is suppressed.
        V1 DECISION (user): ONE single fixed neon accent (e.g. electric cyan)
        shared by EVERY node -- an unambiguous, uniform "activity" status read.
        DEFERRED polish: per-node hue (node's own body colour pushed to max
        saturation/value).
        V1 DECISION (user): STEADY glow, no pulse -- so the tick repaints only
        on state change and the 250ms poll suffices (cheapest variant).
        DEFERRED polish: a gentle BREATHING pulse (phase = monotonic clock,
        ~40-60ms frames while busy via the same self-terminating tick, still
        ZERO idle CPU).
        DONE: paint_processing_halo() = 6 stacked translucent rounded-rects
